---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Icon from "../components/Icon.astro";
import { site } from "../site";

const toc = [
  ["key", "One key, two ways in"],
  ["items", "Each item sealed on its own"],
  ["rollback", "Nothing old comes back"],
  ["remote", "What your sync host sees"],
  ["browser", "In the browser"],
  ["mac", "Around your Mac"],
  ["updates", "Updates you can check"],
  ["limits", "What Satchel can't protect"],
];

const threats = [
  { who: "Someone takes your Mac while it is off or Satchel is locked", ok: "yes", how: "They find sealed files and a key that needs your password or your finger on this Mac." },
  { who: "Your sync host leaks or is broken into", ok: "yes", how: "They get sealed files. No titles, no usernames, no list of the sites you use." },
  { who: "A sync host serves an old copy of your vault", ok: "yes", how: "Satchel notices the older manifest and stops syncing with an error." },
  { who: "A look-alike site asks for your Google password", ok: "yes", how: "Its domain does not match, so the extension offers nothing." },
  { who: "Malware running as you while Satchel is unlocked", ok: "no", how: "It can read what you can read. No password manager survives this. A short auto-lock keeps the window small." },
  { who: "A short master password", ok: "no", how: "Argon2id makes each guess slow and memory-hungry; only a long passphrase makes guessing hopeless." },
  { who: "A forgotten master password", ok: "no", how: "There is no reset and no back door. Write the passphrase down and keep it somewhere safe." },
];
---

<Base title="Security, Satchel" description="How Satchel encrypts your vault, what your sync host sees, how the browser extension decides which site gets which login, and what Satchel cannot protect against.">
  <section class="head wrap stack-lg">
    <h1>How Satchel keeps a secret.</h1>
    <p class="lede">Every choice on this page is in the source code and in the design notes that come with it. Here is the short version, including what Satchel cannot protect you from.</p>
  </section>

  <div class="wrap doc">
    <nav class="toc" aria-label="On this page">
      <ul>{toc.map(([id, label]) => <li><a href={`#${id}`}>{label}</a></li>)}</ul>
    </nav>

    <div class="body">
      <section id="key" class="part">
        <h2>One key, two ways in.</h2>
        <p>When you create a vault, Satchel makes a random 256-bit vault key. That key encrypts everything. Your master password and Touch ID never encrypt items themselves; each one only unlocks a copy of the vault key.</p>
        <div class="pocket keymap" aria-label="Diagram: the password and Touch ID each unlock the vault key, which opens every item">
          <span class="pocket-label">Your Mac</span>
          <div class="slots">
            <div class="slot"><Icon name="key" /><b>Master password</b><small>Stretched by Argon2id: 256 MiB of memory, 3 passes</small></div>
            <div class="slot"><Icon name="fingerprint" /><b>Touch ID</b><small>A Secure Enclave key that cannot leave this Mac</small></div>
          </div>
          <div class="join" aria-hidden="true"></div>
          <div class="vk"><b>Vault key</b><small>256 random bits</small></div>
          <div class="join short" aria-hidden="true"></div>
          <div class="items-row"><span>Logins</span><span>API keys</span><span>Databases</span><span>Notes</span><span>SSH keys</span></div>
        </div>
        <p>So changing your password, or turning Touch ID on, rewraps one small key and re-encrypts nothing. Your password is never stored, not even in the Keychain.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="items" class="part">
        <h2>Each item sealed on its own.</h2>
        <p>Every item is a separate file with a short header and two sealed boxes. Search reads the first box; the second is opened only when you look at or copy a secret.</p>
        <div class="file" aria-label="Diagram of one item file: header, overview box, secret box">
          <div class="cell hdr"><b>Header</b><small>Item id, version and save time, bound to both boxes</small></div>
          <div class="cell ov"><b>Overview box</b><small>Title, username, website, tags</small></div>
          <div class="cell sec"><b>Secret box</b><small>Password, key, one-time-code seed, notes</small></div>
        </div>
        <p>Both boxes use XChaCha20-Poly1305 from libsodium, with a fresh random 192-bit nonce each time an item is saved. The header is authenticated together with the boxes, so it can't be moved onto another item without the change being caught.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="rollback" class="part">
        <h2>Nothing old comes back.</h2>
        <p>Next to the items sits a manifest: the list of every item and its version, with a counter that only goes up, signed with a key derived from your vault key. If a file disappears, is edited, or is swapped for an older one, the manifest no longer agrees.</p>
        <p>When a sync host serves a vault older than the one your Mac last saw, from a restored backup or a host that misbehaves, Satchel stops and tells you. It never quietly brings back a password you changed.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="remote" class="part">
        <h2>What your sync host sees.</h2>
        <div class="seen">
          <div>
            <h3>Gets</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>The vault header, holding the password-wrapped vault key</li>
              <li>The sealed manifest</li>
              <li>One sealed file per item, named by a random id, with its version and the time it last changed</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3>Never gets</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>Your master password or the vault key</li>
              <li>Titles, usernames or the sites you use</li>
              <li>The token or keys Satchel uses to reach it; those live inside the vault</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p>Two Macs can save at the same moment. Satchel writes only if the file is still the version it read, and before using a WebDAV or S3 server it checks that the server really refuses a stale write. A server that doesn't would let two Macs overwrite each other, so Satchel won't use it.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="browser" class="part">
        <h2>In the browser.</h2>
        <ul class="points">
          <li>A page gets only logins saved for its own site, matched by registrable domain with the Public Suffix List.</li>
          <li>Only the page you see is filled, never a frame embedded inside it.</li>
          <li>Nothing is filled without your click or shortcut, and forms are never submitted.</li>
          <li>When you copy a password from the toolbar panel, Satchel copies it. The secret never passes through the extension.</li>
          <li>The Mac app checks the site again itself before it hands over a login. The extension's word is not enough.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section id="mac" class="part">
        <h2>Around your Mac.</h2>
        <ul class="points">
          <li>Copied secrets are marked concealed, so clipboard managers skip them, and the clipboard is cleared after a delay.</li>
          <li>Satchel's windows are left out of screenshots, recordings and screen sharing unless you allow them.</li>
          <li>The vault locks after idle time, on sleep and when the screen locks. Locking wipes the keys from memory.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section id="updates" class="part">
        <h2>Updates you can check.</h2>
        <p>Every release is signed with an Ed25519 key. Your copy of Satchel carries the public half and installs an update only if the signature matches, downloaded only from the project's GitHub releases. An update never opens or changes your vault.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="limits" class="part">
        <h2>What Satchel can't protect.</h2>
        <p>A vault is honest about its edges. Here is who is kept out, and who isn't.</p>
        <div class="threats" role="table" aria-label="Threat model">
          {threats.map((t) => (
            <div class={`threat ${t.ok}`} role="row">
              <span class="mark" role="cell">{t.ok === "yes" ? "Kept out" : "Not covered"}</span>
              <b role="cell">{t.who}</b>
              <p role="cell" class="muted">{t.how}</p>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="part report">
        <h2>Found a problem?</h2>
        <p>Please report it privately through a <a href={site.advisories}>GitHub security advisory</a>, not a public issue. You'll get a reply as soon as possible, and credit in the release notes if you'd like it.</p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .head { padding-block: clamp(32px, 6vw, 72px) clamp(32px, 5vw, 56px); }

  .doc { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 220px 1fr; gap: clamp(32px, 6vw, 88px); padding-bottom: clamp(64px, 10vw, 120px); }
  .toc ul { position: sticky; top: 24px; list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0 0 0 16px; border-left: 1px solid var(--line); display: grid; gap: 10px; font-size: 0.9375rem; }
  .toc a { text-decoration: none; color: var(--moss); }
  .toc a:hover { color: var(--ink); }
  @media (max-width: 860px) { .doc { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } .toc { display: none; } }

  .body { min-width: 0; max-width: 760px; }
  .part { display: grid; gap: 18px; padding-block: 8px 64px; scroll-margin-top: 24px; }
  .part h2 { font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 2.6vw, 2.1rem); }
  .part a { color: var(--saffron-ink); }
  small { color: var(--moss); font-size: 0.8125rem; line-height: 1.4; }

  /* key slots */
  .keymap { display: grid; justify-items: center; margin-block: 12px; padding-block: 40px 32px; }
  .slots { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 16px; width: 100%; max-width: 560px; }
  .slot, .vk { display: grid; gap: 4px; justify-items: center; text-align: center; padding: 16px; border-radius: 14px; background: var(--paper); border: 1px solid var(--line); color: var(--pine); }
  .slot b, .vk b { color: var(--ink); }
  .join { width: 2px; height: 32px; background: var(--pine); opacity: 0.4; }
  .join.short { height: 22px; }
  .vk { background: var(--saffron-soft); border-color: transparent; min-width: 220px; }
  .items-row { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; justify-content: center; gap: 8px; }
  .items-row span { padding: 4px 12px; border-radius: 999px; border: 1px solid var(--line); font-size: 0.875rem; background: var(--paper); }
  @media (max-width: 520px) { .slots { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }

  /* item file */
  .file { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 0.8fr 1.1fr 1.1fr; border-radius: 14px; overflow: hidden; border: 1px solid var(--line); margin-block: 8px; }
  .cell { display: grid; gap: 4px; align-content: start; padding: 16px; }
  .hdr { background: var(--paper); }
  .ov { background: var(--mist); border-inline: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .sec { background: var(--saffron-soft); }
  @media (max-width: 560px) { .file { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }

  .seen { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 16px; }
  .seen > div { padding: 18px 20px; border-radius: 14px; background: var(--paper); border: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .seen > div + div { background: transparent; border-style: dashed; }
  .seen ul, .points { margin: 10px 0 0; padding-left: 1.1em; display: grid; gap: 8px; }
  .points { margin: 0; gap: 12px; }
  .points li::marker, .seen li::marker { color: var(--saffron); }
  @media (max-width: 600px) { .seen { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }

  .threats { display: grid; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .threat { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 110px 1fr 1.3fr; gap: 6px 20px; padding: 16px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); align-items: baseline; }
  .threat p { font-size: 0.9375rem; }
  .mark { font-size: 0.8125rem; font-weight: 650; color: var(--pine); }
  .threat.no .mark { color: var(--saffron-ink); }
  @media (max-width: 680px) { .threat { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }

  .report { padding-bottom: 0; }
</style>
